e showman—he regaled reporters with claims of wild inventions, like a superpowerful “particle beam weapon” that could blast planes from the sky, and drew the curious attention of Mark Twain. More technical than previous biographies, Carlson’s electric portrait might turn off casual readers, but scholars will find it illuminating. 56 photos & 32 illus. (June)\n\nDETAILS\n\nBUY THIS BOOK close\n\nDetails\n\nReviewed on: 04/08/2013\n\nGenre: Nonfiction\n\nCompact Disc - 978-1-4915-3120-4\n\nMP3 CD - 978-1-4915-3144-0\n\nPaperback - 520 pages - 978-0-691-16561-5\n\nPaperback - 520 pages - 978-0-691-29280-9--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTesla: Inventor of the Electrical Age | City Lights Booksellers & Publishers (https://citylights.com/physical/tesla-inventor-of-the-electrical-age-2/)\nciteturn138search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; \n\n### Details\n\nISBN-10: 0691292809\nISBN-13: 9780691292809\nPublisher: Princeton University Press\nPublish Date: 09/15/2026\nDimensions: 7.81\" L, 5.06\" W, 1.16\" H\n\n# Tesla: Inventor of the Electrical Age\n\nbyW Bernard Carlson\n\n#### Paperback\n\nPrice: $19.95\n\n### Overview\n\n“The gold standard for Tesla biography.”–Science\n“Superb.”–Nature\n\nThe definitive account of Tesla’s life and work\n\nNikola Tesla was a major contributor to the electrical revolution that transformed daily life at the turn of the twentieth century. His inventions, patents, and theoretical work formed the basis of modern AC electricity, and contributed to the development of radio and television. Like his competitor Thomas Edison, Tesla was one of America’s first celebrity scientists, enjoying the company of New York high society and dazzling the likes of Mark Twain with his electrical demonstrations. An astute self-promoter and gifted showman, he cultivated a public image of the eccentric genius. Even at the end of his life when he was living in poverty, Tesla still attracted reporters to his annual birthday interview, regaling them with claims that he had invented a particle-beam weapon capable of bringing down enemy aircraft.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTesla: Inventor of the Electrical Age, New TradePaperback | ISBN: 9780691292809 (https://www.hpb.com/tesla-inventor-of-the-electrical-age/P-55569112-NEW.html)\nciteturn138search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 days ago; \n\nImage: Tesla: Inventor of the Electrical Age image number 0\n\n# Tesla: Inventor of the Electrical Age\n\nby Carlson, W. Bernard\n\nISBN: 9780691292809\n\nBe the First! to Submit Reviews\n\nCondition New [Input] $17.03 $14.69 Used [Input] $9.99 $14.99 $7.49 $7.49\n\nFormat CD [Input] $7.49 $7.49 Hardcover [Input] $14.99 Trade Paperback [Input] $9.99 $17.03 $14.69\n\nIdentifier 9780691165615 [Input] $9.99 $17.03 9780691057767 [Input] $14.99 9781491531440 [Input] $7.49 9780691292809 [Input] $14.69 9781491531204 [Input] $7.49\n\nAvailability:\n\n  * Online Only\n\n$14.69\n\n#### Available Offers\n\nCondition New [Input] $17.03 $14.69 Used [Input] $9.99 $14.99 $7.49 $7.49\n\nFormat CD [Input] $7.49 $7.49 Hardcover [Input] $14.99 Trade Paperback [Input] $9.99 $17.03 $14.69\n\nIdentifier 9780691165615 [Input] $9.99 $17.03 9780691057767 [Input] $14.99 9781491531440 [Input] $7.49 9780691292809 [Input] $14.69 9781491531204 [Input] $7.49\n\nSee all editions from\n\nOverview\n\nNikola Tesla was a major contributor to the electrical revolution that transformed daily life at the turn of the twentieth century. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTesla: Inventor of the Electrical Age - W. Bernard Carlson - Google Books (https://books.google.com/books/about/Tesla.html?id=5I5c9j8BEn4C)\nciteturn138search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 13.5 years ago; Crawled: 5 days ago; \nP. Morgan】 January laboratory lamps lecture machine magnifying transmitter manufacture Marconi Martin messages Milutin Morgan Motor Te